.TH OROC-UPDATE-KEYGEN 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.2" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-update\-keygen \- Generate an Ed25519 keypair for signing update manifests.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc update keygen [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Generate an Ed25519 keypair for signing update manifests.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-out=<path>\fR
write keypair JSON to a file instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-id=<id>\fR
optional key identifier to embed in the keypair (default: "pk\-1")
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH NOTES
.PP
The generated JSON includes "keyId", "publicKey", and "privateKey" fields (hex\-encoded). Keep the private key secret; distribute only the public key with your application.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc update keygen > key.json\fR
generate a default keypair and save it to key.json
.TP
\fBoroc update keygen \-\-key\-id pk\-prod \-\-out prod\-key.json\fR
generate a named keypair for production use
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-update(1)
